Source: t70-linux
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ryan Tober <rtober2@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/rtober/t70-linux
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: t70-dsa-dkms
Section: kernel
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: WatchGuard Firebox T70 switch ports (lan3-lan7) as Linux DSA
 Out-of-tree module that bridges the Marvell 88E6176 switch behind the
 I210 at enp4s0 onto the mainline mv88e6xxx DSA driver, so panel ports
 3-7 appear as lan3-lan7. Includes modprobe options, a systemd unit and a
 netplan drop-in (DHCP, optional). Built with DKMS for every installed
 kernel; needs mv88e6xxx from linux-modules-extra.

Package: t70-led
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: WatchGuard Firebox T70 front-panel LED control
 t70-led drives the MODE, ATTN, FAILOVER and STATUS LEDs through the
 Braswell GPIO controller. A systemd unit lights MODE while the OS is up,
 and a timer plus apt hooks blink ATTN while package updates are pending.

Package: t70-poe
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, i2c-tools
Description: WatchGuard Firebox T70 PoE monitor
 t70-poe reads the TI TPS23861 PSE controller over SMBus and prints
 supply voltage, temperature and per-port class, volts, mA and watts for
 panel ports 6 and 7. Monitoring only; the chip powers loads by itself.
